## In Brief
$\pmb{\alpha}$ -ketoglutarate (aKG) is an important cofactor for demethylation reactions that helps to maintain naive pluripotent stem cells. TeSlaa et al. show that at later stages of pluripotency, aKG can promote early differentiation, highlighting that the cellular context and potentially the stage of cellular maturity can alter the effect of aKG.
